The term 'virus', and the associated concept of a program that inserts
itself into host programs, was invented in 1983 by Dr. Fred Cohen. If
I remember _Shockwave Rider_ right, that program was a worm, which
copied itself onto as many computers as it could. David Gerrold used
the term 'virus' for some kind of rogue program in the first edition
of _When Harley Was One_[1].

People were definitely doing tricks and traps on computers practically
from the beginning -- leaving cookie monsters for the night operator
in a mainframe shop, breaking early brittle timesharing system
security to hack each other's terminal sessions, and so on. But I'm
pretty sure the "virus" idea didn't catch on until Cohen.

